      "created_at": "2015-02-28T16:31:31.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Oh hi community!</p><p>This:</p><p>Say both of Sky-Scraper's Rebounding Debilitator cards are placed on the same target. That target then tries to deal 3 or more damage. What happens next? Is it:</p><p>A) Both cards trigger simultaneously. Prevent the instant of damage, then destroy/place on top of the deck both cards in whatever order.</p><p>B) Both cards trigger simultaneously. One of the cards prevents the damage and is destroyed/placed on t.o.d.—the second card \"untriggers\" because there is no longer any damage to prevent, and remains on the target</p><p>C) The cards don't trigger simultanesouly, but in order—same result as B.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I've been going with A. I like the way A feels. Is this wrong?</p><p>Same thing with Neutralizing Resonator: if there are two on one target I would destroy both of them after destroying 1 ongoing, because the \"If you do\" wording seems to allow for a simultaneous destruction trigger. Or is that wrong too?</p><p>How wrong am I?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:03.521Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
